Assume new1.txt does not exist before the following fragment runs inside main() with <stdio.h> included, and that the program may create files in the current directory. What is printed?

FILE *a = fopen("new1.txt", "r");
int x = (a == NULL);
FILE *b = fopen("new1.txt", "a");
int y = (b == NULL);
if (b != NULL)
    fclose(b);
FILE *c = fopen("new1.txt", "r");
printf("%d %d %d", x, y, c == NULL);

